---
description: Two-team color washes put each player's face or team logo on its own color side; headshots fill their rings exactly
globs: src/components/**/*.tsx,src/app/**/*.tsx
alwaysApply: false
---

# Faces sit on their color

Any surface that runs one team color into another (`.matchup-wash`, `.matchup-wash--subtle`, `.score-card-wash`, split bars, left/right tinted panels) must place each side's identity on that side's color:

- Player A's headshot or team A's logo on the left, where A's color is.
- Player B's headshot or team B's logo on the right, where B's color is.
- Never stack or overlap both faces on one side of a two-color wash.
- Values, labels and bars keep the same order: A left, B right.

The wash direction itself is frozen (see `team-wash-gradient-freeze.mdc`). Match the content to the wash, never the other way around.

# Headshots fill their ring

When a `PlayerHeadshot` sits inside a colored ring:

- The ring wrapper is `flex` or `block`, never a bare inline `span` (inline leaves a line-height crescent at the bottom).
- Padding is even on all four sides.
- Pass `className="ring-0"` to the headshot so its default white ring does not show inside the colored one.
